    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35561" root="قرنب" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْنَبٌ</span></b>  The <i>jerboa;</i> or a <i>rat,</i> or <i>mouse;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَأْرَةٌ</span>: or the <i>young one generated between it and a
jerboa:</i> (K:) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فرنب</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِرْنِبٌ</span>, with kesr,]
is a dial. var. thereof. (So in the TA. [But I
incline to think that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْنَبٌ</span> is a mistranscription
for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِرْنِبٌ</span>.])

